cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Judge Bias in a Blind Legal-Advice Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  Six current language models answered sixty legal questions three times
  each, and the same six models graded all 1,080 answers blind against a
  six-dimension safety rubric. The repository holds the pipeline, the
  questions, every answer, all 8,640 grades (6,480 panel grades and 2,160
  grades from two frozen judges), the 2,160 grades of two earlier runs on the
  same questions, and the analysis output. One command recomputes every
  statistic in the accompanying report.
authors:
  - name: edplegal
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/edplegal/llm-legal-reliability-eval"
keywords:
  - LLM-as-judge
  - evaluation
  - legal advice
  - AI safety
  - self-preference bias
  - blinded grading
